### Problem description ###
```text
John has noticed that many of his tweets on Twitter are less than 140 characters long. He wants to make the most of the available space by filling any remaining space with the string 'lolololol' until he reaches 140 characters. For instance, if his message is "What a wonderful day!", he wants to tweet "What a wonderful day!lololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololol". Note that the 'lololol...' part should always end with an 'l'. To achieve this, you may need to leave a space between the message and the start of the 'lolololol...' part. For example, 'Odd' will become 'Oddlololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololol' (without space), and 'Even' will become 'Even lolololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololololol' (with space). Your task is to help John create a function that will take in the string of his message without the 'lololol' part and return a string containing a tweet according to John's specifications.
```

### Prefix ###
```python
nan
```

### Student's incorrect code ###
